# region_actuator.tkr — the scope-local arena routing regressor's HOST (native) assertion.
#
# The program (src/act/act.tks) sums three disjoint weights: 100 (a frame-routed `.next` box reads
# back the value copied into it), 20 (a 4096-cycle churn over that same frame-routed box nets to
# zero), and 135 (an ESCAPING node's box survives its builder's frame drop AND the builder's 4096
# internal churn cycles). The total 255 is the value the VM, the C route and this native route must
# all agree on: a box routed to the wrong region shows up as a corrupted read-back — a wrong total —
# not merely a leak.
#
# The default `When built and run` builds the NATIVE route; the C route and the VM are pinned by the
# self-host gate (`teko test .` and `scripts/diff_vm_native.sh`), and the inversion is re-proven
# under `TEKO_MEM_PARANOID=1` on both routes as part of the ritual.

Feature: region_actuator — a non-escaping local's heap box rides its own scope region, an escaping one the root

  Scenario: the scope-local box routing sums to 255 on the native route
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "255"
